      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221848/assets/3c90c2114f36f77c9bb06c47398f4f5a4ce3b8fc6aadf2a77d28c447a8e424c7.png)\n\nA dilation with center $O$ is defined by the function $(x,y)↦(1.5x,1.5y).$  What is the image of the line shown above under the action of this transformation?",
      "worked_solution": "A dilation leaves a line passing through the center of the dilation unchanged.\n\nTherefore, the image ${l}^{′}$ of the line $l$ under the dilation  $(x,y)↦(1.5x,1.5y)$ is the line $l$ itself, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221848/assets/b48fecb9d9286ac4df6a9bfbf151fd78a98d223f7375e5251cda1119f8f66611.png)",
